„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoHilkiah the second, Tebaliah the third, Zechariah the fourth: all the sons and brethren of Hosah were thirteen.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAmong these were the divisions of the porters, even among the chief men, having wards one against another, to minister in the house of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlAnd they cast lots, as well the small as the great, according to the house of their fathers, for every gate.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And the lot eastward fell to Shelemiah. Then for Zechariah his son, a wise counsellor, they cast lots; and his lot came out northward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=To Obed-edom southward; and to his sons the house of Asuppim.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€To Shuppim and Hosah the lot came forth westward, with the gate Shallecheth, by the causeway of the going up, ward against ward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfEastward were six Levites, northward four a day, southward four a day, and toward Asuppim two and two.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<At Parbar westward, four at the causeway, and two at Parbar.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\These are the divisions of the porters among the sons of Kore, and among the sons of Merari.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd of the Levites, Ahijah was over the treasures of the house of God, and over the treasures of the dedicated things.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€As concerning the sons of Laadan; the sons of the Gershonite Laadan, chief fathers, even of Laadan the Gershonite, were Jehieli.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjThe sons of Jehieli; Zetham, and Joel his brother, which were over the treasures of the house of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHOf the Amramites, and the Izharites, the Hebronites, and the Uzzielites:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMand Shebuel the son of Gershom, the son of Moses, was ruler of the treasures.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And his brethren by Eliezer; Rehabiah his son, and Jeshaiah his son, and Joram his son, and Zichri his son, and Shelomith his son.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÙWhich Shelomith and his brethren were over all the treasures of the dedicated things, which David the king, and the chief fathers, the captains over thousands and hundreds, and the captains of the host, had dedicated.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUOut of the spoils won in battles did they dedicate to maintain the house of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙİAnd all that Samuel the seer, and Saul the son of Kish, and Abner the son of Ner, and Joab the son of Zeruiah, had dedicated; and whosoever had dedicated any thing, it was under the hand of Shelomith, and of his brethren.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlOf the Izharites, Chenaniah and his sons were for the outward business over Israel, for officers and judges.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙàAnd of the Hebronites, Hashabiah and his brethren, men of valour, a thousand and seven hundred, were officers among them of Israel on this side Jordan westward in all the business of the LORD, and in the service of the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙıAmong the Hebronites was Jerijah the chief, even among the Hebronites, according to the generations of his fathers. In the fortieth year of the reign of David they were sought for, and there were found among them mighty men of valour at Jazer of Gilead.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙîAnd his brethren, men of valour, were two thousand and seven hundred chief fathers, whom king David made rulers over the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh, for every matter pertaining to God, and affairs of the king.¦layout ªlast_verse 